sequenceDiagram
    %% ensureService (ts/src/service/client.ts) and startService (service.ts)
    participant door as Front door (archer mcp or CLI)
    participant client as service client
    participant service as archer serve (detached)
    participant account as Account state dir
    participant project as Project checkout
    door->>client: present_diagram, attach_project or start_service
    client->>service: connect archer.sock, hello
    alt a service already answers
        service-->>client: protocolVersion, version, homeUrl
    else nothing listening and auto-start allowed
        client->>service: spawn node archer.js serve --foreground, detached, log to service.log
        activate service
        service->>account: take archer.lock, read service.json (token, port)
        service->>service: bind explicit/configured port or remembered port with free-port fallback
        service->>account: write service.json, new token if the port changed
        loop each project marked attached in runtime/index.json
            service->>account: read runtime recovery record and source blobs
            service->>project: recompile and start a watcher
        end
        client->>service: hello, retried every 50 ms for up to 15 s
        service-->>client: protocolVersion, version, homeUrl
    end
    client->>service: attach root
    service->>project: findProject, ProjectState.open, reload
    service->>account: persist record, mark attached
    service-->>client: root, name, url .../token/p/slug/
    client-->>door: the project page URL
    Note over service: One service per user serves up to 64 projects
    door->>client: stop_service
    client->>service: stop
    service-->>client: stopping
    deactivate service
